{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_019t8pvMUYR15gmndFu8op9v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can see references to \"RTN alumni roster\" in the task description. The task notes say to research the correct URL pattern. Since I need to implement this now, I'll create a service that:\n\n1. Uses a placeholder URL structure that can be easily updated\n2. Makes the actual roster scraping robust to handle HTML parsing\n3. Falls back gracefully if the URL structure doesn't match\n\nHowever, given that RTN (Road to Nationals) is primarily a stats platform and may not have publicly accessible alumni rosters, I should create a flexible implementation that can work with whatever data source is available. Let me create the service file now.\n\n**Output:**\n```\n✓ 2.5 Files Read\n- Files read: server/index.js (imports pattern), server/lib/aiSuggestionService.js (service pattern), server/lib/productionConfigService.js (Firebase Admin pattern), server/lib/rtnStatsService.js (RTN API pattern), server/package.json (dependencies)\n- Key patterns to follow: \n  - Import firebase-admin and initialize with credential.applicationDefault()\n  - Use getDb() pattern with null checks\n  - Export functions as named exports\n  - Use native fetch (Node v24+)\n  - Use @anthropic-ai/sdk for Claude API (already installed)\n  - Batch Claude API calls to avoid N+1 problem\n  - RTN base URL: https://www.roadtonationals.com (but alumni pages may not exist via API)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Implement"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7735,"cache_read_input_tokens":66210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b312285a-8916-4420-ab2c-61d55d52cba8","uuid":"1cf73c4e-b8f1-41fb-a