{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_016KSakP6Pjfr9Qkaor3Z1xc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Output:**\n```\n✓ 7 Status Update\n- PRD status: IN PROGRESS (not updating PRD yet - Phase 4 still has 4 more tasks)\n- Remaining tasks: 11 (Phase 4: 4 tasks, Phase 4-Deploy: 1 task, Phase 5: 6 tasks, Phase 5-Deploy: 1 task, Final-Deploy: 2 tasks)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully completed **Task 4.1: Create talent discovery service**.\n\n### What was implemented:\n\n**File created:** `server/lib/talentDiscoveryService.js`\n\n**Key features:**\n1. **Flexible roster fetching** - Attempts to fetch from RTN with fallback error handling (RTN doesn't have public alumni rosters)\n2. **Batched Claude API scoring** - ALL candidates scored in ONE API call (not N+1) to avoid HTTP timeout\n3. **Fuzzy name matching** - Levenshtein distance algorithm to detect if candidates already exist in roster (85% similarity threshold)\n4. **Social links always null** - Per task requirements, Claude doesn't guess social media URLs\n5. **CandidateCard structure** - Returns: name, school, graduationYear, score (1-5), explanation, linkedIn (null), instagram (null), rtnAthleteId, alreadyInRoster flag\n\n**Important notes:**\n- RTN (Road to Nationals) is a stats platform and doesn't have publicly accessible alumni roster pages\n- The service is designed to be extensible - school-specific URL patterns can be added as needed\n- The implementation prioritizes avoiding API timeouts by batching all Claude API calls\n- Fuzzy matching prevents duplicate entries when names have slight variations\n\n### Next task:\n**Task 4.2: Add talent discovery server endpoint** - Create the API endpoints that call this service and return candidate data to the frontend."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":318,"cache_read_input_tokens":80805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_